  "body": "## Conclusion and credit\n\nAdd the complete certificate and independent mathematical audit for 30005118 / OWR-10252930-031. Same-group cyclic self-sumset recognition is NP-complete in both explicit sparse binary and dense characteristic-vector encodings, already for odd n and nonempty zero-containing targets below n/2. A polynomial-time algorithm in either model exists if and only if P=NP. This is not an unconditional impossibility claim.\n\nInteger NP-hardness and the bounded-universe construction are credited to Abboud, Fischer, Safier, and Wallheimer, *Recognizing Sumsets is NP-Complete*, [arXiv:2410.18661v2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.18661v2), [SODA 2025](https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/1.9781611978322.153). The elementary integer-to-cyclic transfer is supplied in full as a source-applicability argument without a novelty claim. No new hardness gadget construction or full independent audit of the source gadgets is asserted.\n\n## Full proof and audit\n\nThe certificate retains all universal mathematics: normalization with negative and odd minima, zero anchor, absence of 2-torsion, both no-wrap directions, total reduction including empty and zero-diameter cases, sparse bit complexity, dense bounded-universe composition and sparse NP certificate size. The restricted nonempty language uses the explicitly permitted fixed YES replacement (3,{0}). The audit retains every substantive source, mathematical and encoding check and all scope limits.\n\nOnly computational reproduction sections and obsolete or out-of-edition administrative framing are removed. All certificate proof sections and substantive audit sections are byte-identical to their reviewed originals. The source ledger is unchanged. The editions include a precise provenance account and acceptance tied to their actual bytes. AI-assisted and unrefereed; no external human peer review, exhaustive novelty certification or proof-assistant verification is claimed.\n\n## Repository boundary\n\nExactly eight files are added under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30005118/`. No QUEUE.md, existing attempt, unrelated record, historical status or turn count changes. This edition preparation adds no proof-search turn and does not manufacture or reset accounting.\n\nThe packet includes authored proof and audit prose, scoped acceptance and public bibliographic verification metadata only. It excludes source copies or extractions, datasets, private material, scripts, fixtures and standalone outputs. No excluded artifact is transformed into new prose. No merge, release, DOI deposit or external outreach is part of this change.\n\n## Preparation checks\n\nExact editorial differences and byte-preserved mathematical blocks were checked. Public PDF byte/hash identities, UTF-8 and JSON, relative links, manifest, exact allowlist and excluded-material scan passed. The additive patch passed a clean temporary replay with exact path and byte matching. Base Git trees were recomputed and unrelated entries preserved. These are packaging checks, not further mathematical certification; no CI pass is claimed. Exact-head remote readback remains a separate publication check.\n\nBase: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.md`: 2,804 bytes; SHA-256 `15d90535de3b08dc7c2eff6b83d1e26b96bba61ff8eb7d99f5dce467b819751f`\n- `CYCLIC_SUMSET_CERTIFICATE.md`: 11,272 bytes; SHA-256 `7f767eea9e2cf0e8bea67f3762d6116a0ac31d89f64cb2861499ba269d38c3a3`\n- `INDEPENDENT_AUDIT.md`: 6,928 bytes; SHA-256 `2683828c307ecdb427b102fbdd05d8c12b16774f4f2e4660617dcc9da171e319`\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,527 bytes; SHA-256 `e61bf10e64cf497c4ce0d46953eaf631e16da88919c3c982303e3dfac980192c`\n- `PROVENANCE.md`: 3,922 bytes; SHA-256 `6ad164c4f400dbbb704b3856a74fd4778c895fa4a760c5aaa2771886d2991827`\n- `README.md`: 2,574 bytes; SHA-256 `53f14c76b558ab9161d93e4b098321cb376443e74286c8543ed9364bb0f880e8`\n- `SOURCE_LEDGER.md`: 3,386 bytes; SHA-256 `91aad340ab6e86eb4b453dbbc64d52dc504fd84da4e540b08186f3fecf034728`\n- `STATUS.json`: 1,352 bytes; SHA-256 `5046e4e478b6c0d1ecbabd112655f2c0030ca1852f2212b39036d2a8f14e5834`\n\nThe manifest lists eight members and hashes the other seven; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
